Falsifies the `redoxfs_server_session` fuzz target's admission rule.

The defect: the fail-open arm milestone 726 (an unknown badge fails closed in subtree_scope)
removed, restored. `Bindings::of` folds a nonzero badge at or past the table onto badge 0 again, so
a badge the file server has no window for carries the whole endpoint's authority.

Expected to fail: "badge 8 (Revoked) succeeded at op ..." (or badge 18446744073709551615), the
first time a session sends any request the server can satisfy under an unknown badge.

Replay by hand, from the repository root (`script/falsifications` sweeps Kani harnesses and tests,
not fuzz targets):

    git apply fuzz/falsifications/redoxfs_server_session.unknown_badge_fails_open.patch
    mkdir -p /tmp/plant && cargo fuzz run -O redoxfs_server_session /tmp/plant -- -max_total_time=600
    git apply -R fuzz/falsifications/redoxfs_server_session.unknown_badge_fails_open.patch

Measured 2026-10-04 (UTC) on an M-series Mac, from an empty corpus: see notes/fuzzing.md.

